---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { href } from "../lib/paths";
---
<Layout title="Our Care | Kin & Campus">
<div class="w ph"><div class="eyebrow">Our care</div><h1>The plan they already have, held here.</h1><p class="lead">Asthma. ADHD. A thyroid. Anxiety. We keep it going — refills, holidays, finals, a letter home when something changes.</p></div>
<div class="w"><img class="photo" src={href("photos/campus-aerial.jpg")} width="800" height="450" alt="Campus and the surrounding hills, seen from above">
<div class="grid">
<div class="card"><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-heart"/></svg><h3>Chronic care</h3><p>The list you already know stays on track. A local pediatrician holds the plan while they live here.</p></div>
<div class="card"><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-moon"/></svg><h3>A trained eye nearby</h3><p>Check-ins around holidays, finals, and the week they get back from break. Someone looking after them, in town.</p></div>
<div class="card"><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-clock"/></svg><h3>Same-day sick visits</h3><p>A doctor who already knows them. Same week, and usually same day.</p></div>
<div class="card"><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-leaf"/></svg><h3>Health literacy now</h3><p>How to call a doctor. How to keep a plan. How to notice a dip. They learn care while they're young — not at forty.</p></div>
<div class="card"><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-compass"/></svg><h3>Hometown doctor in the letter</h3><p>Named on day one. Copied when it counts. May note home; August starts from a full page.</p></div>
<div class="card"><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-chat"/></svg><h3>A number they actually have</h3><p>Direct physician text. A real person in Blacksburg, eight minutes from campus.</p></div></div></div>
<section><div class="w split"><svg class="art" viewBox="0 0 360 360" role="img" aria-label="Portrait placeholder"><rect width="360" height="360" rx="28" fill="#EADFCB"/><circle cx="180" cy="140" r="56" fill="#9CAF98"/><path d="M70 330q110-150 220 0z" fill="#6B2737"/><circle cx="270" cy="86" r="20" fill="none" stroke="#C9A24B" stroke-width="8"/></svg>
<div><div class="eyebrow">The physician</div><h2>A board-certified pediatrician. Local to Blacksburg.</h2><p class="lead">A pediatrician who already lives in this town, knows the drive from campus, and built the panel for Virginia Tech students — and for the parents still 250 miles away.</p><p>Looking after them here, in lockstep with the doctor at home. Eight minutes from campus. Direct text. A letter the same afternoon.</p><h3 style="margin-top:28px">How I practice</h3><p>I sit with the student. You get the standing rule you agree on. Their hometown doctor gets the note the same afternoon. These are the years they learn how to be a patient.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding-top:0"><div class="w"><div class="eyebrow">A year in town</div><h2>Holidays, finals, the Sunday they get back.</h2><div class="grid"><div class="card"><div class="num">August</div><p>Parent conversation. Then the student meets their doctor — long enough to start together.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="num">The semester</div><p>Sick days, yes. Also holidays, finals, the Sunday they get back from break.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="num">Finals</div><p>A check-in on sleep, stress, and how the plan is holding.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="num">May</div><p>A note home. The hometown physician has the year. August starts from a full page.</p></div></div>
<p style="margin-top:36px"><a class="btn" href={href("join")}>Reserve a spot</a></p></div></section>
</Layout>
